  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "Evidence: The strongest results (0.706–0.725) all come from the scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile recipe, with transformer aggregation + weighted fusion (config_017, 0.725) as the best. All four aggregation×fusion combinations for that recipe are now tested. Question: config_045 (scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) isolates the image-encoder contribution by swapping imagenet_vit_l for resnet50 while keeping the best RNA encoder, aggregation, and fusion. This clarifies how much of the 0.725 accuracy is attributable to the ViT-L image encoder versus the other components. Why this is the best last experiment: No remaining untested configuration uses the full winning recipe (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile), so beating 0.725 is very unlikely. Among remaining options, config_045 has the highest expected accuracy because it retains 3 of the 4 winning components. It also provides a useful ablation for the study. Expected cost is moderate (~3–4 GPU hours, slightly cheaper than config_017's 3.60 h since resnet50 is smaller than ViT-L), keeping total budget reasonable."
}

